reshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","notes":"RIGOR (reported, MAJOR — a sign error, verified numerically). The block displays Phi_q(z) = prod_{k>=1} (1 - q^{-k} z)^{-1} and then says 'Using the expansion Phi_q(z) = exp[ sum_{k>=1} z^k / (k(1 - q^k)) ]'. The two disagree: the correct exponent for the displayed product is sum_{k>=1} z^k / (k(q^k - 1)), i.e. the sign of the denominator is flipped. Derivation: -log prod_{k>=1}(1 - q^{-k}z) = sum_{k>=1} sum_{m>=1} q^{-km} z^m / m = sum_m (z^m/m) * q^{-m}/(1 - q^{-m}) = sum_m z^m / (m (q^m - 1)). Checked numerically at q_0 = 1.1099785827513808 and z = 0.3 (mpmath, 30 dps, product to k = 4000): the product is 19.1252192245359338, exp[sum z^k/(k(q^k-1))] = 19.1252192245359338 (agreeing to 30 digits), while the block's exp[sum z^k/(k(1-q^k))] = 0.05228698234826454 — its RECIPROCAL, wrong by a factor of 366 at this point. The stated expansion is the correct one for the OPPOSITE convention prod(1 - q^{+k} z)^{-1} with |q| < 1, which is presumably where it was copied from. This is load-bearing: the very next sentence says 'each evaluation unpacks into a series of Plancherel-weighted Markov traces', and that unpacking runs through this exponent. Proposed: z^k / (k(q^k - 1)). SEE ALSO the batch note on Phi_q convention drift — prf:phi-q-tower-algebraic-stratification in this same batch writes Phi_q as prod_{n>=0}(1 - q^n x), with no inverse, positive powers of q, and index from 0: three differences from the product displayed here.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"fail","severity":"major","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","notes":"Proposed (NOT applied inline — deleting it removes the one